e is all their  enemies the reason armin thinks of this  flashback is because if aaron seriously  wanted to kill everyone outside the  island then that would explain why he'd  want to have distance between him and  his childhood friends an act of violence  on this scale is something that's never  been done in human history so by aaron  pushing them away neither armin or  mikasa would bear any of the  responsibility or the guilt for his  actions that being said armin basically  changes the subject to mucus's headaches  earlier in the episode she mentioned how  these headaches were evidence of her  lacking free will since erin claimed  acumens only get these when their true  self is trying to resist their  programming his point was that mikasa  only wants to protect him because her  dna is forcing her to but armin argues  that aaron was lying and used his  pre-existing knowledge about the  headaches to make this lysy more legit  the two of them then agree to simply ask  him about it once everything is over and  the scene cuts to above ground where the  man himself is quite literally fighting  for his life having already been shot in  the head by mcgath and stabbed through  the shoulder with a spike of his own  hardening the attack titan still  relentlessly tries to win the fight he  gets the armor titan to back off by  triggering another set of spikes out the  ground and ryan himself even starts to  wonder what aaron is fighting for and  why he keeps on struggling the answer to  that question is that besides having an  unusual level of willpower aaron knows  that once he horizon shiganchena like  they agreed the simple act of them  making contact would win the battle  that's why it was smart of him to stay  in fight instead of trying to escape  like elena wanted him to since the odds  would instantly shift in their favor  once his brother gets there we then get  this hilarious sequence of galileo  pouncing onto aaron only to get slapped  halfway across the gachana and if i was  porco i'd just give it up at this point  because when it comes to this match up  he can't ever seem to deal the finishing  blow  luckily for the warriors reiner catches  the attack titan off guard only a few  seconds later and as he pins aaron down  he thinks to himself how he just wants  this to be done  from the start of the season rhino has  had the aura of someone who is mentally  exhausted by the constant fighting and  suffering that he's been through which  is why he can't understand why aaron  continues to fight despite all the odds  being against him the attack titan  demonstrates his persistence again by  grabbing the warrior's upper draw and  just using brute force to try and rip it  off and considering he's the one being  pinned down this is a pretty impressive  feat of strength the scream he let out  while doing it was so loud that it  almost acted like an sos signal since  zeke and the remaining jaegers had just  made it back to the wall the beast tyson  then reintroduces himself by launching a  pitching assault directly at reiner's  head and amazingly this isn't even the  first time he's wrecked the armored  titan in shiganjina  following that he takes out chunks of  hardening from the wall and sends it  flying towards mali's airships and the  destruction of these ships is a big deal  because it means the forces on the  ground have one less thing to worry  about what was really impressive about  this moment though was that after doing  two pitching assaults in a row zeke was  already geared up to do a third which he  directed at the car titan  in this scene the most important thing  for the beast was that he launched this  shot before magath had a chance to fire  the anti-titan cannon otherwise this  fight might have been over there and  then  as you can tell mcgath was desperate to  punish zeke for betraying mali and i  think a lot of his resentment comes from  the fact that as the former head of the  warrior unit he never once realized that  zeke was secretly working against them  it is true to say that he did consider  zeke to be a mysterious person but still  i imagine it hurts him to know that this  betrayal happened from someone that he  allowed to become a warrior  anyhow with the card titan hanging off  the wall and the aegis approaching pique  had no other option but to run it's  actually implied that they chased her  around nearly the whole length of  shiganjina since here she was on zeke's  left side but by the end of the episode  she was on his right side meaning she  likely would have gone the long way  around  a weekend aaron then starts limping  towards his brother so they can make  contact while on the ground gabby and  cole decide to go and find falco  although colt didn't want her to come  gabby was on a mission to repay her  fellow warrior candidate since the only  reason falco is in a cell with zeke's  spinal fluid inside him is because he  kept saving her on different occasions  inside the cell he has a conversation  with nile who's another person that's  been contaminated and in this moment it  seemed like he accepted he's not going  to see his family again  unlike irvin who is willing to abandon  this idea of having a family to pursue  his dream nile always considered his  wife and daughters to be the most  important thing hence why he took that  stand against the nobles in season 3.  for that reason it is especially  heartbreaking that he's been put in the  situation but later in the episode nile  at least did what he could to reunite  falco with his family  as the scouts and the aegis free more  and more prisoners pixies begins to  organize them and he decides that those  without black armbands will get what's  left of the odm gear while those with  the armbands will fight on the front  lines this was the most logical way of  doing things considering that you know i  mean people with the armbands could be  titanized by zika any time so it'd be a  waste of equipment to give them odm gear  only for them to then become pure titans  as a side note instructor shard has made  his first appearance since flock had him  beaten up by the cadets but due to his  injuries that may or may not actually be  bear related he told connie to go on  without him in the changing room mikasa  gets suited up for battle with her  number one fan louise and as she  mentions they are now fighting for  similar goals again the last time these  two interacted louise was in a cell  after helping flock and the yeagaris to  leak information but since then the  political situation has obviously  flipped with the old leaders of the  island either being dead or not doing so  great  an interesting detail is that mikasa  chose to leave her scarf behind and this  could mean a couple of things for  example it could be because she's still  questioning whether her attachment to  aaron is off her own free will or  perhaps she just left it because she's  still seriously hurt by him saying he  hated her either way it's clear that  regardless of whether aaron was telling  the truth about these things he still  succeeded in creating distance between  them by making mikasa doubt her own  feelings  on the outside yelena is genuinely the  happiest person on the island because as  far as she's concerned this is about to  be the moment when the euthanization  plan becomes a reality the scouts  themselves then come out at just the  right time to get a good view of  everything and jon starts to question  what happened to levi and hanji he knew  the captain would have never let zeke go  of his own free will and yelena  correctly assumes that the beast titan  defeated him although to be fair he was  super lucky not to have died in the  process  now in spite of this armin tries to  motivate everyone to help the yeager  brothers make contact since he believes  more than anyone else that aaron is  secretly on their side in armin's head  he thinks that eren will trigger a small  rumbling using the titans in shiganjina  whereas obviously yana believes that the  first thing aaron will do is remove the  ability of aldians to reproduce although  they do think different things will  happen they do essentially still have  the same goal which is to reunite aaron  and zeke hence why armin wants to  actively help the aegirus we then get  this moment from jonada where she pulls  one of the weirdest faces we've seen  from either a titan or a human in fact  it was so terrifying that mikasa  actually went to grab her sword in terms  of the reason behind why she pulled his  face i mean there are two reasons here  firstly there's the real life reason  which is that i kind of think this  moment was meant to be a jumpscare kind  of thing and the second reason is that  yelena was trying to figure out army's  true intentions  prior to this armin cried when she told  him about the euthanization plan and  although he tried to pretend like he was  in favor of it in his own mind he  clearly thought that aaron would never  go along with it therefore it's possible  that yelena wasn't really sure if she  believed that he was being genuine but  now having stared deep into his soul she  has faith that he is really on her side  moving down to ground level colt and  gabby were on the search for falco and  the eldest warrior candidate was armed  with both a regular rifle and an  anti-titan rifle this rifle is good for  killing pure titans if you can get a  direct hit on the nape but when it comes  to shifters it's highly unlikely to do  any damage evidenced by this brief  exchange earlier in the episode  as they continue to search the streets  colts and falco then catch a glimpse of  each other and like i mentioned earlier  nile willingly reunites the two brothers  what was interesting about this  interaction was that colt was bracing  himself to shoot now because he didn't  really have a choice but it was gabby  who instinctively held him back if this  had happened a month ago i mean she  